@startuml
title UC-01 Report Campus Issue

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #DCEEFF
  ParticipantBorderColor #4B8CCB
  ActorBackgroundColor #DCEEFF
  ActorBorderColor #164B78
  LifeLineBorderColor #8EABBF
  GroupBackgroundColor #EEF4F8
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #DCEEFF
  BorderColor #4B8CCB
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8E8
  BorderColor #D9B867
}

actor "Reporter" as reporter
participant "Web Frontend" as web
participant "API Gateway" as gateway
participant "Auth Service" as auth
database "Photo Storage\n(uploads volume)" as photo_volume
participant "Ticket Service" as ticket
database "Ticket DB\n(PostgreSQL)" as ticket_db

autonumber

reporter -> web : Select "Report Issue", enter category, location,\ndescription and attach 1-5 photos
web -> gateway : POST /api/tickets (multipart, Bearer JWT)
activate gateway
gateway -> auth : POST /auth/session (verify token)
auth --> gateway : claims (role REPORTER)
gateway -> gateway : Validate required fields and photos\n(1-5 files, max 5 MB each, JPEG/PNG/WebP)
break invalid token (401), not a signed-in Reporter (403), missing field or invalid photo (400)
  gateway --> web : error response
  web --> reporter : Show error, ticket not created
end
gateway -> photo_volume : Save photos
photo_volume --> gateway : photo URLs (/uploads/...)
gateway -> ticket : gRPC CreateTicket(category, location, description, photoUrls)
activate ticket
ticket -> ticket_db : One transaction: INSERT ticket (status SUBMITTED)\n+ status history + outbox event
ticket_db --> ticket : committed
ticket --> gateway : ticket {id, status SUBMITTED}
deactivate ticket
gateway --> web : 201 Created
deactivate gateway
web --> reporter : Show Ticket ID and status "Submitted"
note over gateway, ticket_db : The ticket is now listed in the Central Admin inbox (UC-02).\nWith AUTO_ROUTING_ENABLED=true the same transaction also queues a routing job,\nand a matching category rule can assign the ticket before an admin does.

== Alternate flow: Reporter cancels a "Submitted" ticket ==
reporter -> web : Cancel ticket
web -> gateway : DELETE /api/tickets/{id}
activate gateway
gateway -> ticket : gRPC CancelTicket(id), after checking the ticket is the caller's
activate ticket
ticket -> ticket_db : One transaction: status CANCELLED + history + outbox event
ticket --> gateway : ticket CANCELLED
deactivate ticket
gateway --> web : 200 OK
deactivate gateway
web --> reporter : Ticket removed from the normal list
@enduml
